<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Pawawoi Karaeng Sigeri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1911</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Pawawoi Karaeng Sigeri was king of Bone in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a> from 1895 to 1905. He refused <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> demands for control of Bone's ports and revenues, and in 1905 a Dutch expedition conquered the kingdom. He was captured after a campaign in the interior and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandung">Bandung</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, where he died. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> later named him a National Hero.</p></div>
